---
devlanes runs a dev environment per Git worktree (a lane) with its own ports, URLs and env. Call the devlanes tool with the command line after "devlanes" as args.
- Run dev servers, watchers, workers and tunnels with exec: `devlanes exec --name web -- pnpm dev`. devlanes owns the process and gives it the lane's ports and env. Never use &, nohup or a background shell for them.
- start, restart and wait block until ready or failed: no sleep or curl polling.

More:
- Read a unit with `devlanes logs web --tail 100`, the lane with `devlanes status`, a failure with `devlanes debug why web`.
- Run builds, tests, git and other commands that exit in your own shell, or with `devlanes with -- pnpm test` when they need the lane running.
- Stop what you started with `devlanes stop --mine`. Leave the lane running when you hand work to the user for review.
- Commands that delete data or reach other machines ask the user first.
- cwd picks the worktree; without it the call uses the project the agent runs in.
